The test builds `raw_member` with `status="restricted"`, a nested user dict, `until_date` as an integer timestamp, `can_send_media_messages=False`, and the other permission flags. In `ChatMember.de_json`, when called on `ChatMember`, the `"status"` value is popped and used to dispatch to `ChatMemberRestricted.de_json`, so the subclass receives the remaining dict. That method converts `user` via `de_json_optional(..., User, bot)`, converts `until_date` via `from_timestamp` using the bot defaults timezone (`Asia/Kathmandu`), then for `ChatMemberRestricted` specifically it pops `can_send_media_messages` into `api_kwargs` and calls `super()._de_json(...)`; because this is a classmethod on the subclass, `_de_json` receives `cls` as `ChatMemberRestricted` and `data` as the mutated dict after those conversions and pop operations.

